# REQUIRES: python-api
# Per-type sigma and epsilon tunable on a table with an NBFIX of
# [ nonbond_params ] (D213, maintainer's decision on PR #159):
# the pair CT-OW keeps its values, and an update during a run equals, to the
# bit, a compile with the rule's values for the other pairs and the NBFIX's
# own, on the CPU against a NumPy sum of the Lennard-Jones.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide nbfix CPU Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,NUMPY
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide nbfix CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU {{Double|Mixed}}: NBFIX kept: an update at step 6 and 10 steps equal a compile with the new values from that state to the bit
# NUMPY: NBFIX: the change of the energy at fixed positions
# CHECK: nbfix passed
